INTRO = """You are the writer of unit {unit} of the Scrapkeep structure sweep. Scrapkeep is a Godot 4.7.2 GDScript game under `sketches/core-loop` with a Node toolchain under `scripts/`. The sweep removes duplicate code, wrong-way dependencies and private reach-ins without changing anything a player or a test can observe.

## Read first

Run `git fetch origin`. The sweep's own pages live on the branch `origin/entropy/records`, not on your base, so read them with `git show`:
1. `git show origin/entropy/records:project-guide/handoff/STRUCTURE-SWEEP.md`, the section "Rules for every writer". Those rules bind you: hard limits, set up, work order, checks and hand in. Follow them exactly.
2. {findings}
3. `git show origin/entropy/records:adr/TADR-012-script-dependency-loops.md`, which explains lint rule L16.
Also read `AGENTS.md` and `sketches/core-loop/ARCHITECTURE.md` in your checkout. A survey finding can be wrong in detail, and line numbers have moved since the survey: confirm each finding in the code before you change anything, and report any that is not as described.

## Base and branch

Base commit: `{base}` (a pushed tip of `origin/entropy/gate`). Branch: `{branch}`. Your checkout may start on another commit: create your branch from the base as the set-up section says (`git switch -c {branch} {base}`), and stop with `BLOCKED` if `git rev-parse HEAD` does not print the base afterwards.

## The unit

All paths are under `sketches/core-loop/` unless they start with `scripts/`. {body}

For every change: find every caller first (`git grep`, including `.tscn`, `.tres`, `tools/`, `tests/` and string calls such as `call("name"`), weigh at least two options, and take the one that leaves the least code and adds no new layer. If the cheapest option for one item still adds more code or indirection than the dependency it removes is worth, leave that item and say so with the reason: a left item with a reason is a good result, a forced fix is not. Do not merge two things that only look alike: compare copies with `diff` and merge only what gives the same result for every input. When a new call or a new home replaces an old one, move every caller in the same commit and delete the old one; old and new never live side by side, and no forwarding copy stays behind. Add no code comments (the repo's rule in `CONTRIBUTING.md`, "Editing conventions"). No test may be deleted or weakened; a test changes only to follow a moved or renamed call. Never edit any `package.json`; a new Node test goes inside a test file that `npm test` already runs (read the `"test"` line of the root `package.json`), never in a new `*.test.mjs` file. The repo tracks a `.gd.uid` file beside every script: a moved script moves with its `.uid` file (`git mv` both), and a new script gets one from a Godot import run, committed with it.

Lint rules: `npm run sketch:lint` fails if a file joins a dependency loop (L16) and if a script under `src/` holds a mutable `static var` that `tools/test_batch_driver.gd` does not reset (L14). If the lint prints `BASELINE <path>:1 <rule> ... no longer offends: remove from baseline`, remove exactly that entry from `scripts/sketch-lint.baseline.json`. Never add an entry there{baseline_exception} and never pass `--write-baseline`. A `static var` that moves to a new file gets a reset registered in `tools/test_batch_driver.gd` in the form the driver already uses, not a new baseline entry.

Formal models: the files `src/core/flow.gd`, `src/core/profile.gd`, `src/core/progress.gd`, `src/world/event_director.gd`, `src/combat/combat.gd`, `src/presentation/audio.gd`, `src/presentation/ace_sequencer.gd` and a few others are covered by formal models (`.agents/skills/scrapkeep-verify-formal/SKILL.md` lists them). This machine has no Java, so do not run the model checker. If you change a covered file, say in your report exactly which lines changed, so the coordinator can update the models' sync notes.

Done looks like: {done}

Guard: {guard}

Other units are in flight. Do not edit their files beyond a line a rename or a moved path forces, and list every such line in your report: everything under `src/build/`, `src/boss/` and `src/movement/` (a build, boss and movement unit); everything under `src/combat/` and `src/presentation/enemy_clips.gd` (a combat unit); under `src/world/`: `terrain.gd`, `event_director.gd`, `activities.gd`, `camp_hub.gd`, `world.gd`, `map_gorge.gd`, and the files under `events/`, `park/` and `pockets/` (a world unit, which also renames `_press` in `src/ui/screens.gd`); the five files `adversity_director.gd`, `dynamic_setpieces.gd`, `encounter_engine.gd`, `env_tags.gd` and `refurbished_elites.gd` under `src/experimental/` (a unit waiting on the owner). {siblings}

## Checks

Start every shell line with `export PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH GODOT_BIN="$HOME/Applications/Godot_4.7.2.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot"`, and run Godot only with `HOME` set to a scratch folder under `artifacts/local/` as the rules page says. One `npm run sketch:fast -- --base {base}` after your last commit. It picks tests from the changed files; make sure the tests the findings name and those found by `{testgrep}` ran, and if any did not, run them in one more call with `--test` (on this repo `--test` replaces the automatic selection, so that second call is in addition to the first, not instead of it). Then `npm run sketch:lint`{extra_checks}. Run every command in the foreground to completion; never end your turn while a command runs. `npm run sketch:fast` may wait several minutes for a machine slot before it starts: that is normal, wait for it, and make one call rather than several. A known failure that is not yours: `tests/profile_purity_test.gd` and `tests/slice1_patch_and_w1_craft_test.gd` are red on the base; say so if they show, and rerun any other red alone before you call it red. Do not start sub-agents.

## Hand in

As the rules page says: push, open a draft pull request against `entropy/gate` titled `{unit}: ...`, and end your final message with the line `PR <full URL>, head <SHA>, checks and reviews <state>`. Lead with `PASS`, `ISSUES` or `BLOCKED`. For each part say what changed and give the `git grep` output that shows the old form is gone; list anything you left, with the reason. If the push is declined, do not try another way: report `BLOCKED` with the local commit SHA. Name your model and effort in the receipt.
"""

